{
  "dom_id": "step-q325131",
  "name": "Question 18",
  "problem": "The weekly exercise time for a community is normally distributed with a mean of $\\mu $ minutes and a standard deviation of $30$ minutes. Additionally, $60%$ of people exercise between $0.9\\mu $ minutes and $1.1\\mu $ minutes each week. Find the percentage of people who exercise less than $220$ minutes per week. **Round your answer to two decimal places.**\n\n*Hint: A table of values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p$ is given below, where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $p$ | $\\,0.75\\,$ | $\\,0.80\\,$ | $\\,0.85\\,$ | $\\,0.90\\,$ | $\\,0.95\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,0.6745\\,$ | $\\,0.8416\\,$ | $\\,1.0364\\,$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n*In addition, you're given the following table of values for $p=Φ(z)$*.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-1.2\\,$ | $\\,0.1020\\,$ | $\\,0.1003\\,$ | $\\,0.0985\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.1\\,$ | $\\,0.1210\\,$ | $\\,0.1190\\,$ | $\\,0.1170\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.1423\\,$ | $\\,0.1401\\,$ | $\\,0.1379\\,$ |\n\nApproximately\n{{field-1}}$%$ of the people exercise less than $220$ minutes per week.",
  "worked_solution": "Let $X$ represent the weekly exercise time of a randomly selected person. Then we have $X∼N(\\mu ,{30}^{2}),$ and we want to find $P(X<220).$ But first, we need to find the mean $\\mu .$ \n\nWe know that $P(0.9\\mu <X<1.1\\mu )=0.60.$ First, we convert this to a cumulative probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0.9\\mu <X<1.1\\mu ) & =0.60 \\\\ 2P(\\mu <X<1.1\\mu ) & =0.60 \\\\ P(\\mu <X<1.1\\mu ) & =0.30 \\\\ P(X<\\mu )+P(\\mu <X<1.1\\mu ) & =0.5+0.30 \\\\ P(X<1.1\\mu ) & =0.80\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we convert $X$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<1.1\\mu ) & =0.80 \\\\ P(Z<\\frac{0.1\\mu }{30}) & =0.80 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{0.1\\mu }{30}) & =0.80 \\\\ \\frac{0.1\\mu }{30} & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.80).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, \n\n$$\n{Φ}^{-1}(0.80)=0.8416.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{0.1\\mu }{30} & =0.8416 \\\\ 0.1\\mu  & =25.248 \\\\ \\mu  & =\\frac{25.248}{0.1} \\\\  & ≈252.48.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve for $P(X<220)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<220) & =P(Z<\\frac{220-252.48}{30}) \\\\  & ≈P(Z<-1.08) \\\\  & =Φ(-1.08) \\\\  & =0.1401 \\\\  & ≈14.01%\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, approximately $14.01%$ of the people exercise less than $220$ minutes per week.",
